<title>USA: Countrywide unit files $1 bln debt shelf.</title>
<headline>Countrywide unit files $1 bln debt shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Countrywide Home Loans Inc, a unit of Countrywide Credit Industries Inc, filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $1 billion in guaranteed medium-term notes.</p>
<p>Underwriters for the shelf offering are Lehman Brothers, Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, JP Morgan &amp; Co, Nationsbanc Capital Markets Inc, Salomon Brothers Inc and Countrywide Securities Corp.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes, the company said in the filing.</p>
</text>
